From ccb3b4eb7ce037820b0cf04203c89370d6a6bf77 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Guild-Idler Patch Tool <patch@guild-idler.local>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 22:13:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 0249: Hero Comparison table

New 'Compare Heroes' button on the Heroes tab -- sortable table of
every hero's gear score, quest/raid win rates, and lifetime gold/xp
earned. Genuinely new tracking, not a display change -- the only
per-hero counter that existed before this was questsCompleted
(attempts, quest-only, no raid tracking at all).

Five new lifetime counters on Hero: questsSucceeded, raidsParticipated,
raidsSucceeded, goldEarnedLifetime, xpEarnedLifetime. SAVE_VERSION
50->51, migration 50 backfills all five to 0 for existing saves --
no prior history to recover any of this from.

Quests/chains/chain-replays covered for free via QuestManager.resolve's
single shared code path. Raids needed real new wiring in
RaidManager.resolve: success = the same fullClear condition already
used for completedRaids/titles; gold/xp split evenly across the party
rather than full-credited to everyone, so a 6-hero raid doesn't look
like it multiplied a hero's earning power by 6x.

Gear Score needed zero new tracking -- HeroManager.gearScore(hero)
already existed, called live in the table.

UI: sortable modal table behind a new chip, shown once there's more
than one hero. Quests/Raids show won/attempted (pct%), not a bare
count. New .hero-compare-table CSS matching .craft-picker-table's
existing conventions.

Verified: npx tsc --noEmit and npx vite build both pass clean against
the properly re-based tree. Confirmed RaidManager's party size can
never be 0 at the point of the gold/xp division. SAVE_VERSION chain
contiguous (49->50->51).
